1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,640
Business Case 11 begins when a version-pinned onboarding plan generates
cross-functional work.

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:11,280
Day-one readiness is derived from reconciled new-hire, manager, IT and
facilities evidence.

3
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,630
The governed record is NHR-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:18,800
The accountable actors are New Hire, People Operations, Manager, IT,
Facilities.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:25,850
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:30,537
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 5 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:30,537 --> 00:00:38,972
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:43,659
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:43,659 --> 00:00:46,629
Process 1, People Operations: Generate dependency-aware plan.

10
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:53,418
The action assign plan and owners produces cross-functional tasks and
critical path in the Onboarding ledger.

11
00:00:53,418 --> 00:00:56,389
Process 2, New Hire: Complete private work.

12
00:00:56,389 --> 00:01:03,178
The action submit forms and documents produces completion or correction
receipt in the Private evidence store.

13
00:01:03,178 --> 00:01:05,724
Process 3, Manager: Complete manager readiness.

14
00:01:05,724 --> 00:01:12,089
The action confirm agenda, goals and buddy produces manager readiness
evidence in the Onboarding ledger.

15
00:01:12,089 --> 00:01:15,908
Process 4, IT and Facilities: Fulfil access and workplace.

16
00:01:15,908 --> 00:01:22,273
The action complete or retry requests produces provisioning and
facilities receipts in the Fulfilment ledger.

17
00:01:22,273 --> 00:01:25,244
Process 5, People Operations: Reconcile critical path.

18
00:01:25,244 --> 00:01:32,033
The action inspect blockers and evidence produces ready or explicitly
blocked projection in the Analytics store.

19
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:34,758
The actual product route is /hr/onboarding/analytics.

20
00:01:34,758 --> 00:01:40,208
It presents dependency-aware onboarding readiness in the surrounding
recruitment or onboarding workspace.

21
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:51,562
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

22
00:01:51,562 --> 00:01:54,312
The seeded workbench follows record RDY-DEMO-001.

23
00:01:54,312 --> 00:02:08,518
Its governed fields are Plan, OBP-DEMO-001 , template v6; Critical
tasks, 9 total , 7 reconciled; New-hire tasks, 4/4; Manager tasks, 2/2;
IT/Facilities, 1/3 blocked; Day-one readiness, 78% , critical blocker.

24
00:02:08,518 --> 00:02:17,226
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

25
00:02:17,226 --> 00:02:21,062
With People Operations selected, we perform recalculate day-one
readiness.

26
00:02:21,062 --> 00:02:25,751
The guard requires every critical dependency has a current
completion/effect receipt.

27
00:02:25,751 --> 00:02:40,244
The state changes from Blocked · 2 critical items to Ready · evidence
reconciled, records DayOneReadinessCalculated, writes to the Onboarding
evidence ledger, and creates the handoff: Manager and new hire see
updated critical path.

28
00:02:40,244 --> 00:02:44,689
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate IT fulfilment
failure.

29
00:02:44,689 --> 00:02:50,024
The prepared failure is Laptop shipment and directory account are
partially fulfilled.

30
00:02:50,024 --> 00:02:59,359
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

31
00:02:59,359 --> 00:03:07,007
The owned recovery is Retry fulfilment and reconcile.

32
00:03:07,007 --> 00:03:16,568
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

33
00:03:16,568 --> 00:03:28,996
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

34
00:03:28,996 --> 00:03:50,985
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through critical-path readiness, overdue work and exception age and
minimum-context next-actor work.

35
00:03:50,985 --> 00:03:53,252
Business Case 11 is complete.

36
00:03:53,252 --> 00:04:06,401
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

37
00:04:06,401 --> 00:04:11,841
Day-one readiness is derived from reconciled new-hire, manager, IT and
facilities evidence.

38
00:04:11,841 --> 00:04:16,829
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
